  "slug": "generalizable-horuseye-119d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers extend single-cell embeddings to multi-omic, proteomic and spatial settings with explicit claims of transferability across…",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learning single-cell representations that transfer across modalities, platforms and datasets rather than being tuned to one experiment. scpFormer pre-trains a transformer on over 390M cells and embeds variable antibody panels through ESM and value-aware encoding, while SCIGMA integrates up to five spatial omics modalities with uncertainty-aware contrastive learning. Other preprints pursue the same integration problem by different routes: scDisent separates expression and regulation latents with a sparse causal module, and the CITE-seq tensor method applies HOSVD for parameter-free, interpretable RNA and ADT integration. What is new is the emphasis on interpretability and uncertainty, including attention maps in the 3D bag-of-visual-words pipeline and FeatureMAP's gene-level contribution and variation trajectories. The published items pursue related goals, but no shared benchmark links the set, so the convergence is a tendency rather than a shared result.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-22"
}
